+    /// The record the move would leave behind crosses the byte ceiling its shape is written
+    /// under ([`flat_value_ceiling_crossed`] for a flat record,
+    /// [`segment_value_ceiling_crossed`] for a segment record): refused **before anything at all
+    /// was written**. Unlike [`Self::Conflict`] it is not transient — it fails again every pass
+    /// until the record shrinks, so it is an operator signal rather than a retry.
+    Refused {
+        /// The re-encoded record's own length.
